44A.—(1) For the purposes of section 25F(1) of the Act, a person who intends to appeal against a notice to maintain served under section 25E(4) of the Act may file an appeal in accordance with paragraph (2).
(2) The appeal must —
(a)be addressed to the Permanent Secretary, Ministry of National Development;
(b)be sent by email to MND_HQ@mnd.gov.sg;
(c)contain —
(i)a summary of the grounds of appeal; and
(ii)a succinct presentation of the appellant’s arguments of fact or law supporting each ground of appeal; and
(d)be accompanied by a copy of the following documents:
(i)the notice to maintain served on the appellant;
(ii)any other correspondence between the appellant and the Commissioner of Building Control in relation to the notice to maintain;
(iii)any other document supporting the ground of the appeal or argument of fact or law.
[S 616/2025 wef 01/10/2025]
